    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d504-a5">

                <pb facs="0797" n="669" xml:id="pg669"/>

                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1885-07-03"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 3,
                        1885</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Consul-General</hi>: The President of the United
                    States of America directs me to express to you his sincere thanks, and those of
                    the people of the United States, for great attention shown by you to the parties
                    sent in search of the survivors of the Jeannette Arctic exploring expedition,
                    and the respect and honors paid by you to the remains of Lieutenant-Commander De
                    Long and his comrades, as they passed through Russia on their way to their
                    native land.</p>
                <p>Be pleased to accept, Mr. Consul-General, the assurances of my distinguished
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer><signed>T. F. BAYARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Mr. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edmund De Lagrené</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Consul-General of France, Moscow.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
